/-- Law-level coordinate-congruence bridge for Hansen's chi-square-normalized
inverse-Wishart scalar.

Once the transformed scalar has a target law and the realized Wishart matrices
are nonsingular a.s., the deterministic congruence theorem transports the law
back to the original coordinates. This is the probability wrapper used before
the full Wishart whitening/rotation law transport is available. -/
theorem inverseWishartScaledLinearForm_hasLaw_of_congr_inverse
    (W : Ω → Matrix m m ℝ) (Sigma : Matrix m m ℝ) (α : m → ℝ)
    (T S : Matrix m m ℝ) (ν : Measure ℝ)
    (hST : S * T = 1) (hTS : T * S = 1)
    (hSigma : IsUnit Sigma.det)
    (hW_nonsing : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, IsUnit (W ω).det)
    (hLaw : HasLaw
      (fun ω =>
        inverseWishartScaledLinearForm (Tᵀ * Sigma * T) (Tᵀ *ᵥ α)
          (Tᵀ * W ω * T)) ν μ) :
    HasLaw (fun ω => inverseWishartScaledLinearForm Sigma α (W ω)) ν μ :=
  hLaw.congr <| by
    filter_upwards [hW_nonsing] with ω hW
    exact (inverseWishartScaledLinearForm_congr_of_inverse
      Sigma (W ω) α T S hST hTS hSigma hW).symm

