/-- Orthogonal coordinate changes preserve Hansen's chi-square-normalized
inverse-Wishart scalar form, once `Σ` and the realized Wishart matrix are
nonsingular.

This bridge packages the inverse and quadratic-form algebra needed to reduce a
general fixed direction to a rotated coordinate direction. -/
theorem inverseWishartScaledLinearForm_orthogonal_congr
    (Q : Matrix m m ℝ) (Sigma : Matrix m m ℝ) (α : m → ℝ)
    (W : Matrix m m ℝ)
    (hSigma : IsUnit Sigma.det) (hW : IsUnit W.det)
    (hQTQ : Qᵀ * Q = 1) (hQQT : Q * Qᵀ = 1) :
    inverseWishartScaledLinearForm (Qᵀ * Sigma * Q) (Qᵀ *ᵥ α)
        (Qᵀ * W * Q) =
      inverseWishartScaledLinearForm Sigma α W := by
