/-- **Hansen Theorem 11.11**, raw inverse-Wishart scalar endpoint.

This is the textbook raw form: `(α'W⁻¹α)⁻¹` has the distribution of
`χ²(n-m+1)/(α'Σ⁻¹α)`, once the normalized Schur-complement map identity has
been supplied. -/
theorem inverseWishartLinearForm_hasLaw_theorem11_11_raw
    (W : Ω → Matrix m m ℝ) (Sigma : Matrix m m ℝ) (α : m → ℝ)
    (hW : HasLaw W (wishartLaw (n := n) Sigma) μ)
    (hmap : (wishartLaw (n := n) Sigma).map
        (inverseWishartScaledLinearForm Sigma α) =
      chiSquared (Fintype.card n - Fintype.card m + 1))
    (hscale_ne : α ⬝ᵥ (Sigma⁻¹ *ᵥ α) ≠ 0) :
    HasLaw (fun ω => inverseWishartLinearForm α (W ω))
      ((chiSquared (Fintype.card n - Fintype.card m + 1)).map
        fun x => (α ⬝ᵥ (Sigma⁻¹ *ᵥ α))⁻¹ * x) μ :=
  inverseWishartLinearForm_hasLaw_scaled_chiSquared_of_scaled
    (W := W) (Sigma := Sigma) (α := α)
    (df := Fintype.card n - Fintype.card m + 1)
    (inverseWishartScaledLinearForm_hasLaw_theorem11_11
      (W := W) (Sigma := Sigma) (α := α) hW hmap)
    hscale_ne

